# Brief: "Explain our OIDC login to a new backend engineer. They keep asking
# which redirect happens when."
#
# Thesis: the browser makes three hops, and the application never sees the
# user's password.
#
# Focal path: top to bottom - this is a sequence, the order IS the message.
# Layout: none. Sequence diagrams ignore the layout engine.
# Medium: internal docs.
#
# Deliberately one flow: no refresh, no logout, no error branch. Those are three
# more sequence diagrams, not three more branches on this one - a sequence
# diagram with conditionals in it stops being readable at about two.

...@../../styles/minimal-light

shape: sequence_diagram

user: User {class: actor}
browser: Browser {class: secondary_service}
app: Application {class: primary_service}
idp: Identity Provider {class: external_system}

user -> browser: click "Sign in"
browser -> app: GET /login
app -> browser: 302 to IdP (+ state, PKCE challenge)
browser -> idp: GET /authorize
user -> idp: credentials + MFA
idp -> browser: 302 back with code
browser -> app: GET /callback?code
app -> idp: POST /token (code + verifier)
idp -> app: id_token + access_token
app -> browser: session cookie
browser -> user: signed in
